Independently check the memo lead/writer/work/memo-2026-10-12.md against the notes file and every criterion below. Do not edit the memo. Report findings and REQUIRED CHANGES (verbatim, if any) in your report summary, details in a file in your own work/ directory. Check every Due value against the notes (resolve each date yourself), check every commitment in the notes (including informal ones said in passing) has a row, check every decision, check section order and the 'Summary:' first line, and count words yourself. List any item you cannot judge, or any criterion that can be read two ways, as 'ambiguous' (do not decide it). End your report with the coverage lines: 'criteria met: n of m' and 'n of m factual claims verified'.

Client rulings on due dates: a date the notes give for an event the action is for (e.g. 'book the room for Oct 14') is the Due; 'before Friday' means that Friday's date (inclusive); 'this week' with no hard date, or no date at all, is 'none'; a deadline relative to another dated event in the notes (e.g. 'the day before the freeze starts') is that resolved date. No 'Open questions' section allowed.

Regression list (client rejections, verbatim):
- R1: "No, not right yet. Always start the memo with a one-line 'Summary:' of the meeting, then the decisions, then the action items."

## Acceptance criteria
C1: The memo covers only the meeting in the named notes file.
C2: Every decision stated in the notes file appears in the memo's Decisions section, and no decision appears that the notes do not state.
C3: Every commitment in the notes file appears as a row in the Actions table, including informal ones said in passing without an ACTION label (anything a person said they would do), each with the person who committed to it as Owner.
C4: Actions are a markdown table with exactly the columns Owner | Action | Due.
C5: Due is an ISO date (YYYY-MM-DD) when the notes state a date or give a deadline that can be resolved from the meeting date (for example 'before Friday'); otherwise Due is 'none'.
C6: At most 400 words.
C7: The reviewer's report shows every criterion met (criteria met: n of m with n = m), and the writer applied every required change.
C8: The memo starts with a one-line 'Summary:' of the meeting, followed by the Decisions section, then the Actions (action items) table, in that order.
Plus regression list R1 (above).

